22nd X AI: reject a provider type change that keeps the stored API key (multi-tenant mode).
Upstream already rejects a changed api_base or custom_config. A new provider type also
sends the stored platform key to another endpoint, so it needs a new key too (HTTP 400).
Covers PUT /api/admin/llm/provider, POST /api/admin/llm/test and the image generation
config update, which keeps the stored key of the old provider.
Apply from the backend/ export root: patch -p1 --forward --batch --fuzz=0 < 0002-llm-provider-type-key-guard.patch

